## Task workspace

This project manages its work with Task (`taskcode`; `task` and `tc` are aliases). Task records, documents, decisions and handoffs live in `{{workspacePath}}/` as Markdown files with YAML frontmatter. Read `{{workspacePath}}/README.md` for how the tool works.

- Create and change tasks through the CLI (`task create`, `task update <id> --status in-progress`) rather than keeping a separate TODO list. Do not hand-edit `id`, `status_history` or other managed frontmatter.
- Use `--json` for machine-readable output; commands exit non-zero on failure, and outside an interactive terminal they require explicit arguments instead of prompting.
- When starting work in a git repository, use `task start <id> --track` so `task changes <id>` can show what the task changed.
- Deleting is recoverable only briefly: `task delete <id> --yes` moves items to the OS temp folder; restore with `task undelete <trash-id>`. Prefer `task archive` for work that should be kept.
- Run `task validate` after editing anything inside `{{workspacePath}}/`. Every Markdown file there needs valid frontmatter.
- Record meaningful decisions in `{{workspacePath}}/decisions/` and agent handoffs in `{{workspacePath}}/handoffs/`.
